e\\\" (recent books of interest) | |\\n| Jun2011 | Illuminations | \\\"Editors' Choice\\\" (recent books of interest) | |\\n\\nOxford-Weidenfeld Translation Prize\\n\\nThe annual Oxford-Weidenfeld Translation Prize is an award recognizing \\\"book-length literary translations into English from any living European language ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_awards_and_honors_received_by_John_Ashbery\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d36\"},\"ref\":\"d36\",\"snippet\":\" ... She was shortlisted for the 2016 Scotiabank Giller Prize for The Party Wall, which is an English translation of her French-language short story collection Le mur mitoyen. Leroux won the 2019 Governor General's Literary Award for English to French translation for her translation of Do Not ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/the-top-20-canadian-books-of-2024-so-far-1.7252475\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d37\"},\"ref\":\"d37\",\"snippet\":\" ... English-language novels\\nCategory:American LGBTQ novels\\nCategory:American children's novels\\nCategory:2015 children's books\\nCategory:Children's books with transgender themes\\nCategory:LGBTQ-related children's novels\\nCategory:2010s LGBTQ novels\\nCategory:Scholastic Corporation books\\nCategory:Stonewall Book Award–winning works\\nCategory:Censored books\\nCategory ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melissa_(novel)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d38\"},\"ref\":\"d38\",\"snippet\":\" ... The 2022 National Book Awards Longlist: Translated Literature\\nauthor: The New Yorker\\ndate: 2022-09-14\\n---\\nThis week, The New Yorker will be announcing the longlists for the 2022 National Book Awards. This morning, we presented the ten contenders in the category of Young People's Literature. Check ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.newyorker.com/books/page-turner/the-2022-national-book-awards-longlist-translated-literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d39\"},\"ref\":\"d39\",\"snippet\":\" ... Selected Prose, 1971-2001 (2002) earned the Truman Capote Award for Literary Criticism, the largest annual prize for literary criticism in the English language. John Carey in the London Sunday Times proposed that Heaney's \\\"is not just another book of literary criticism…It is a record of ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.poetryfoundation.org/poets/seamus-heaney\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d40\"},\"ref\":\"d40\",\"snippet\":\" ... Phenomena like climate change, biodiversity loss, deforestation or soil erosion, she says, \\\"actually look very different when you take into account different languages, different historical memories and different cultural frameworks of understanding.\\\" This is a central tenet of the environmental humanities, the multidisciplinary field that Heise has helped ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.biophilia-fbbva.es/en/noticias/ursula-heise-storytelling-awareness-environmental-crisis-biophilia-award/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d41\"},\"ref\":\"d41\",\"snippet\":\" ... It has been translated into 50 languages. The most for any author, dead or alive.\\n\\nIn 2005, Time magazine named the \\\"milestone in African literature\\\", Achebe's magnum opus, one of the 'best 100 English language novels written since 1923' — the year Time was founded.\\n\\nThings Fall