n| Pierre Béarn | 1902–2004 | 102 | French poet |\\n| Pepin Bello | 1904–2008 ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_centenarians_(authors,_editors,_poets_and_journalists)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d28\"},\"ref\":\"d28\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Known World won the Pulitzer Prize for Fiction in 2004 and the International Dublin Literary Award in 2005.\\n\\nEdward P. Jones is an award-winning American author and short story writer. His first short story collection, Lost in the City, won the PEN/Hemingway Award and was ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d56\"},\"ref\":\"d56\",\"snippet\":\" ... Personal prizes\\n\\nIn 2006, Murakami became the sixth recipient of the Franz Kafka Prize.\\n\\nIn January 2009, Murakami received the Jerusalem Prize, a biennial literary award given to writers whose work deals with themes of human freedom, society, politics, and government. There were protests in Japan and elsewhere ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haruki_Murakami\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d15\"},\"ref\":\"d15\",\"snippet\":\" ... His eight books of poetry include Weather Permitting (1999), which was shortlisted for the Irish Times Poetry Prize; Exemplary Damages (2002), and New and Selected Poems (2004). His latest collection of poems, Reality Check (2007), was shortlisted for the Irish Times / Poetry Now Prize in 2008. A selection ... \",\"title\":\"https://griffinpoetryprize.com/judges/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"9f2c5a1f1bf57d367fdc9cf804abad7b16484c397e8993fd12039614b95e2ddc\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"959a3f7cf1c6c5630813be4922bf5e1c7cf8ad8c33e123452d5e1352846c0fab\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"literary prize founded 2004 2005 2006 2007 2008 2009\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d57\"},\"ref\":\"d57\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2000\\n\\nSci Fi Award Nominees\\n\\n2017, 2016, 2015, 2014, 2013, 2012, 2011, 2010\\n\\n2009, 2008, 2007, 2006\\n\\nScience Fiction By Decade:\\n\\n1930s, 1940s, 1950s, 1960s, 1970s,\\n\\n1980s, 1990s, 2000s, 2010s, 2020s\\n\\nScience Fiction By Year:\\n\\n2020\\n\\n2019, 2018, 2017, 2016, 2015, 2014, 2013, 2012, 2011, 2010\\n\\n2009\\n\\nNew ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.goodreads.com/list/show/4893.Best_Science_Fiction_of_the_21st_Century\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d58\"},\"ref\":\"d58\",\"snippet\":\" ... at BeingCharlieKaufman.com\\n* \\n* \\n* \\n* Susan Orlean's original article for The New Yorker\\n* Adaptation, Shooting Script, by Charlie Kaufman, Spike Jonze. Nick Hern Books, 2002. .\\n\\nCategory:2002 films\\nCategory:2002 comedy-drama films\\nCategory:2000s American films\\nCategory:2000s English-language films\\nCategory:American black comedy films\\nCategory:American ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adaptation_(film)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d59\"},\"ref\":\"d59\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2014, 2013, 2012, 2011\\n\\nNew Speculative Writers by Decade:\\n\\n2000s, 2010s\\n\\nScience Fiction By Ratings:\\n\\n100,000 and more, 50000 to 99999, 25000 to 49999, 10000 to 24999\\n\\n1000 to 9999, 100 to 999, Less than 100\\n\\n192 books ·\\n\\n230 voters ·\\n\\nlist created April 4th, 2020\\n\\nby Mitchell ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.goodreads.com/list/show/146613.Science_Fiction_2020_2029_\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d60\"},\"ref\":\"d60\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2006, Gene Luen Yang's graphic novel American Born Chinese, originally published as a webcomic on Modern Tales, was the first graphic novel to be nominated for a National Book Award.Bosman, Julie. (October 12, 2006). \\\"National Book Award Finalists Chosen\\\". The New York Times, Pg. E2 ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Webcomic\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d61\"},\"ref\":\"d61\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2003-04-24\\n---\\nThe decade of the 2000s in film involved many significant developments in the filmmaking industries around the world, especially in the technologies used. Building on advancements from the 1990s, computers were widely utilized to create effects that would have previously been more expensive and time ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2000s_in_film\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d62\"},\"ref\":\"d62\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2000s.\\n\\nCINEMABLEND NEWSLETTER\\n\\nYour Daily Blend of Entertainment News\\n\\n97. Cloverfield (2008)\\n\\nThe first decade of the Aughts saw one word playing into many of its most cherished cinematic successes: reinvention. For director Matt Reeves' Cloverfield, two different types of genre favorites were mashed together to create a ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cinemablend.com/movies/the-100-best-movies-of-the-2000s\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d63\"},\"ref\":\"d63\",\"snippet\":\" ... Due to a lack of interest, McNett shut Big Panda down in 2000. Chris Crosby, who ran his webcomic Superiosity on Big Panda at the time, contacted McNett in order to create a new webcomics portal, which resulted in Keenspot. This new portal became a major success.\\n\\nIn ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_webcomics\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d64\"},\"ref\":\"d64\",\"snippet\":\" ... He could do a bit of everything on the field, and had numerous NCCAA awards to make another compelling case for an all-decade team.\\n\\nTim Fanus: Fanus was an NCCAA All-American that was known for grit and work ethic. He was staple of the early 2000 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cairnhighlanders.com/news/2021/6/16/mens-soccer-announces-2000s-all-decade-team.aspx\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d65\"},\"ref\":\"d65\",\"snippet\":\" ... See Tons of New Marvel Legends Figures\\\". Marvel Entertainment. Retrieved February 26, 2019.\\n\\nAwards\\n\\n* National Cartoonists Society Comic Book \\\"Reuben\\\" Awards\\n**1998 National Cartoonists Society Comic Book \\\"Reuben\\\" Award for Superman: Peace on Earth.\\n**2022 National Cartoonist Society Reuben Award Best Graphic Novel Nominee (Pending), Fantastic Four: Full ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alex_Ross\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d66\"},\"ref\":\"d66\",\"snippet\":\" ... In any event, The Corrections won the 2001 National Book Award and the James Tait Black Memorial Prize and was one of the biggest bestselling novels of the decade.\\n\\nAlice Munro, Runaway (2004)\\n\\nHonestly, I might have put Hateship, Friendship, Courtship, Loveship, Marriage (2001) here, or The View ... \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/a-century-of-reading-the-10-books-that-defined-the-2000s/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"71c98adadc2466a97c9369446878aac8e56604ef7f594dd079787f325e8d2ca2\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"09097c7436f92cbad579da49132a5b7667d176c26beb1aa8dd8bab2640208761\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"new book award created 2000s decade\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d67\"},\"ref\":\"d67\",\"snippet\":\" ... Allan Bromley Prize in Biomedical Engineering (2000)\\n\\nTHE D. ALLAN BROMLEY PRIZE IN BIOMEDICAL ENGINEERING (2000) is awarded to a Senior who has exhibited superior accomplishment and scholarly achievement in Biomedical Engineering.\\n\\nD. Allan Bromley Prize in Environmental Engineering (2000)\\n\\nTHE D. ALLAN BROMLEY PRIZE IN ENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEERING ... \",\"title\":\"https://secretary.yale.edu/services-resources/lectureships-fellowships-and-prizes/department-prizes\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d6\"},\"ref\":\"d6\",\"snippet\":\" ... Established by Barbara Kingsolver in 2000 and funded entirely by her, it is awarded biennially to the author of a previously unpublished novel of high literary caliber that exemplifies the prize's founding principles.\\n\\nThe PEN/Faulkner Award for Fiction is a national prize which honors the best ... \",\"title\":\"https://americanwritersmuseum.org/literary-links/literary-awards/?srsltid=AfmBOooYIGTV-EUbGd9xDLmBUtcV_Ts9VM7oqhh4K0lfwTLcUoKmITFg\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d68\"},\"ref\":\"d68\",\"snippet\":\" ... Times by Linda Grant (2000); An American Marriage by Tayari Jones (2019)\\n\\n7. America Award\\n\\nThe America Award was established in 1994 to recognize lifetime achievements in writing. Part of its mission is to offer an alternative to the famous Nobel Prize in Literature.\\n\\nEach year, a jury ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.tckpublishing.com/prestigious-literature-awards/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d69\"},\"ref\":\"d69\",\"snippet\":\" ... They also offer awards, including the Raymond Souster Award. Top prizes range from $300 to $2000.\\n\\nLush Triumphant Literary Awards\\n\\nThe awards, offered by subTerrain, are for fiction, poetry, and nonfiction. The cost to enter is $30 and awards $3000 in prizes.\\n\\nMarilyn Baillie Picture Book Award\\n\\nThis ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.dreamerswriting.com/writing-contests-in-canada/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d70\"},\"ref\":\"d70\",\"snippet\":\" ... History\\n\\nThe Akutagawa Prize was established in 1935 by Kan Kikuchi, then-editor of Bungeishunjū magazine, in memory of author Ryūnosuke Akutagawa. It is sponsored by the Society for the Promotion of Japanese Literature, and is awarded in January and July to the best serious literary story published ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akutagawa_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d51\"},\"ref\":\"d51\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Paris Peace Conference of 1919 and Its Attempt to End War | 2002 | | |\\n\\nSee also\\n\\n* British literature\\n* English literature\\n* List of years in literature\\n* List of literary awards\\n* Prizes named after people\\n\\nNotes\\n\\nReferences\\n\\nExternal links\\n\\n* \\n* \\n* \\n\\nCategory:1999 establishments in the United Kingdom\\nCategory:Awards established in 1999 ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baillie_Gifford_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d26\"},\"ref\":\"d26\",\"snippet\":\" ... Nobel Prize in Literature\\n\\nnobelprize.org\\n\\nThis award is one of the most prestigious in the field of literature. It's awarded based on overall remarkable contribution. Presented annually since 1901, the Swedish Prize was established as per the will of Alfred Nobel. Writers are nominated for the ... \",\"title\":\"https://rocketexpansion.com/book-awards/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d71\"},\"ref\":\"d71\",\"snippet\":\" ... List of couples awarded the Nobel Prize - Wikipedia\\ndate: 2022-08-19\\n---\\nThe following is a list of couples who were awarded and nominated for the Nobel Prize.Nobel Prize-awarded couples nobelprize.org The latest couple to receive the Prize were Abhijit Banerjee and Esther Duflo for ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_couples_awarded_the_Nobel_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d49\"},\"ref\":\"d49\",\"snippet\":\" ... Midnight Robber (2000) was shortlisted for the James Rl Tiptree Jr. Memorial Award in 2000 and nominated for the Hugo Award for Best Novel in 2001. Skin Folk (2001) received the World Fantasy Award and the Sunburst Award for Canadian Literature of the Fantastic in 2003. The Salt ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.yorku.ca/laps/huma/canadian-writers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d72\"},\"ref\":\"d72\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her 4-volume series Daibu!! (Dive!!, 2000–2002, winner of the Shogakukan Award for Children's Literature) has been adapted into a manga series, a feature film and a TV anime series.\\n\\n136. 2006 No prize awarded\\n\\n131-1. 2004 Hideo Okuda b. 23 October 1959\\n\\nTrapeze (空中ブランコ ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.goodreads.com/topic/show/22206030-winners-of-the-naoki-prize\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"17ae9c9a8b6372c088c44cd8d7103fd0420385a81f94dbc71dfd802512165bb0\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"bf0c1cb2301e30bcbb84af8660052436a11ba49cca381183e1a1111ee505755f\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"award established 2000s literature prize\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_415e75766be144eeb8e5ded7"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the puzzle. The International Booker Prize was established in 2005 (2000s). Let me think about this more carefully. The puzzle says Book A was \"later in contention\" for the award. Let me look at the International Booker Prize winners in the 2010s and think about which books were translated into 25+ languages.\n\nLet me look at the International Booker Prize page and its winners.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d14\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_612594b896e04502bb0bce40","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"International Booker Prize winners list 2010s by year\", \"Man Booker International Prize winners 2016 2017 2018 2019\", \"International Booker Prize winning books authors 2010s\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_0e0f0706e6ff45eca2c87e00","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d14\",\"document_chars\":27249,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"8ce61c1087f7e5edc11d95aa8c819ec764b2f8d2e4c5ab64aaa81fda45d083cf\",\"snapshot\":\"25e42c9d9629a06063929aefe4e8f050cac2c095d797b7476410c1a6fe277c5a\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: Booker Prize - Wikipedia\\nauthor: Authority control databases National Germany United States France BnF data Czech Republic Israel\\ndate: 2001-10-18\\n---\\nname: The Booker Prize\\nawarded_for: Best work of sustained fiction of the year, written in English and published in the UK or Ireland\\nreward: £50, 000\\npresenter: Booker, McConnell Ltd (1969–2001), Man Group (2002–2019), Crankstart (2019 onwards)\\nlocation: Somerset House, Strand, London, England\\nyear: 1969\\nimagesize: 150px\\n\\nThe Booker Prize, formerly the Booker Prize for Fiction (1969–2001) and the Man Booker Prize (2002–2019), is a prestigious literary award conferred each year for the best single work of sustained fiction written in the English language, which was published in the United Kingdom or Ireland. The winner of the Booker Prize receives , as well as international publicity that usually leads to a significant sales boost. When the prize was created, only novels written by Commonwealth, Irish and South African (and later Zimbabwean) citizens were eligible to receive the prize; in 2014, eligibility was widened to any English-language novel—a change that proved controversial.\\n\\nA five-person panel consisting of authors, publishers and journalists, as well as politicians, actors, artists and musicians, is appointed by the Booker Prize Foundation each year to choose the winning book. Gaby Wood has been the chief executive of the Booker Prize Foundation since 2015.Gaby Wood at The Booker Prizes.Jennifer (20 April 2015), \\\"Booker Prize Foundation Hints at New Direction with Appointment of Gaby Wood as Literary Director\\\", Books Live, Sunday Times (South Africa).\\n\\nA high-profile literary award in British culture, the Booker Prize is greeted with anticipation and fanfare around the world. Literary critics have noted that it is a mark of distinction for authors to be selected for inclusion in the shortlist or to be nominated for the \\\"longlist\\\".\\n\\nA sister prize, the International Booker Prize, is awarded for a work of fiction translated into English and published in the United Kingdom or Ireland. Unlike the Booker Prize, short story collections are eligible for the International Booker Prize. The £50,000 prize money is split evenly between the author and translator of the winning novel.\\n\\nHistory and administration\\n\\nThe prize was established as the \\\"Booker Prize for Fiction\\\" after the company Booker, McConnell Ltd began sponsoring the event in 1969; it became commonly known as the \\\"Booker Prize\\\" or the \\\"Booker\\\". Jock Campbell, Charles Tyrrell and Tom Maschler were instrumental in establishing the prize.\\n\\nWhen administration of the prize was transferred to the Booker Prize Foundation in 2002, the title sponsor became the investment company Man Group, which opted to retain \\\"Booker\\\" as part of the official title of the prize. The foundation is an independent registered charity funded by the entire profits of Booker Prize Trading Ltd, of which it is the sole shareholder. The prize money awarded w\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":3000,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_612594b896e04502bb0bce40"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d14\"},\"ref\":\"d14\",\"snippet\":\" ... Forty years later, the Booker Prize Foundation announced in January 2010 the creation of a special award called the \\\"Lost Man Booker Prize\\\", with the winner chosen from a longlist of 22 novels published in 1970. The prize was won by J. G. Farrell for Troubles, though the ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d10\"},\"ref\":\"d10\",\"snippet\":\" ... Readers' Poll, 1999\\n\\n2000-2010:\\n\\n- Best Local Author, NOW Magazine Readers' Poll, 2000\\n\\n- Winner Booker Prize for The Blind Assassin, 2000\\n\\n- Nominated for the Orange Prize, 2001\\n\\n- International Crimewriters Assocation Dashiell Hammett Award, 2001\\n\\n- Canadian Booksellers Association People's Choice Award, 2001\\n\\n- Short-listed for the IMPAC Dublin ... \",\"title\":\"https://margaretatwood.ca/awards-recognitions/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d29\"},\"ref\":\"d29\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2002-08-11\\n---\\nThe following is a list of winners and shortlisted authors of the Booker Prize for Fiction. The prize has been awarded each year since 1969 to the best original full-length novel, written in the English language, by a citizen of the Commonwealth of Nations ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d73\"},\"ref\":\"d73\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2022-02-20\\n---\\nThe Booker in the 2010s\\n\\n2010-19: New Frontiers\\n\\nThe 2010s were a hugely significant decade for the Booker, largely due to the shift in rules which came into place in 2014. From that year onwards, the Prize was open to all novels published in ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ontheprize.co.uk/blog/the-booker-prize-in-the-2010s\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d27\"},\"ref\":\"d27\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2014. \\\"Nominees, Winners, and Losers.\\\" Journal of Cultural Economics 38(4):291–313. [Google Scholar]\\n\\n- Goff Martyn. 1989. Prize Writing: An Original Collection of Writings by Past Winners to Celebrate 21 Years of the Booker Prize. London, UK: Sceptre. [Google Scholar]\\n\\n- Grazian David. 2005. Blue Chicago: The Search ... \",\"title\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10837049/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d74\"},\"ref\":\"d74\",\"snippet\":\" ... List 2012 . International IMPAC Dublin Literary Award 2012. Retrieved 23 January 2015.\\n* Financial Times 2010 Fiction of the YearBlau, Rosie (3 December 2010). FT Fiction Round-up 2010. Financial Times, Fiction Round-up 2010. Retrieved 25 January 2015.\\n\\nLife of Pi\\n\\n* Winner of the 2002 Man Booker Prize ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yann_Martel\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d75\"},\"ref\":\"d75\",\"snippet\":\" ... For the past twenty-five years, Sarah McGrath has shepherded many books to phenomenal success—including best-seller lists and recognition by the Booker Prize, National Book Awards, and Pulitzer Prize, among others—at Knopf, Scribner, and, since 2006, Riverhead Books. Her illustrious list of authors includes Brit ... \",\"title\":\"https://centerforfiction.org/grants-awards/medal-for-editorial-excellence/medal-for-editorial-excellence-past-recipients/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d9\"},\"ref\":\"d9\",\"snippet\":\" ... The novel features three female narrators and takes place fifteen years after the character Offred's final scene in The Handmaid's Tale. The book was the joint winner of the 2019 Booker Prize.\\n\\nNonfiction\\n\\nIn 2008, Atwood published Payback: Debt and the Shadow Side of Wealth, a ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Atwood\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d76\"},\"ref\":\"d76\",\"snippet\":\" ... The decade—and the Australian phase of Carey's career—culminated with the publication of Oscar and Lucinda (1988), which won the Booker McConnell Prize (as it was then known) and brought the author international recognition. Carey explained that the novel was inspired, in part, by his time ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Carey_(novelist)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d77\"},\"ref\":\"d77\",\"snippet\":\" ... Last year's Booker winner, Sri Lankan writer Shehan Karunatilaka, came to us courtesy of the smallest publisher ever to win the prize, husband-and-wife indie Sort Of Books. In 2022, all the glittering literary prizes went to indies – not only the Booker, but its sister prize ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/16/uk-indie-publishing-mavericks-shook-up-books-booker-nobel-fitzcarraldo-sort-of-books-daunt\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"eddebacf3fe38b97b84d