ion trilogy.\\n\\nEnglish novelist Pat Barker was born in 1943. She is the author of the prize-winning Regeneration trilogy. The last book in the series, The Ghost Road, won the Booker Prize in 1995. Her latest novel, The Silence of ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d73\"},\"ref\":\"d73\",\"snippet\":\" ... Booker in the 2010s\\nauthor: Eyes\\ndate: 2022-02-20\\n---\\nThe Booker in the 2010s\\n\\n2010-19: New Frontiers\\n\\nThe 2010s were a hugely significant decade for the Booker, largely due to the shift in rules which came into place in 2014. From that year onwards, the Prize ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ontheprize.co.uk/blog/the-booker-prize-in-the-2010s\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d76\"},\"ref\":\"d76\",\"snippet\":\" ... The decade—and the Australian phase of Carey's career—culminated with the publication of Oscar and Lucinda (1988), which won the Booker McConnell Prize (as it was then known) and brought the author international recognition. Carey explained that the novel was inspired, in part, by his time ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Carey_(novelist)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d81\"},\"ref\":\"d81\",\"snippet\":\" ... First Book Award | — | | |\\n| 2009 | The Rehearsal | Montana New Zealand Book Awards | First Book Award | | |\\n| 2009 | The Rehearsal | Orange Prize | — | | |\\n| 2010 | The Rehearsal | Amazon.ca First Novel Award | — | | |\\n| 2013 | The Luminaries | Booker Prize | — | | None |\\n| 2013 | The Luminaries | Governor General's Awards | English-language fic